222,111
**Minor · new: the two-year gross-hiring claim lacks its primary series.** The [built page](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/dist/events/jobs/2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000/index.html) quotes “A Labor Department measure of gross hiring” as having “been stuck in a rut for more than two years.” The quotation matches the pinned [AP record](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/coverage/ap-september-jobs.txt). The pinned [August JOLTS release](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/bls-jolts-2026-08.txt) says “Hires changed little at 5.2 million,” while the available, unpinned [BLS historical hires series via FRED](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/graph/fredgraph.csv?id=JTSHIL&cosd=2024-06-01&coed=2026-08-01) contains `2024-06-01,5137` and `2026-08-01,5192`. AP is accurately credited, but the pinned release alone does not let a reader check the two-year characterization.

VERDICT: SHIP
